<title>POLAND: May weather favourable for Polish crops - ministry.</title>
<headline>May weather favourable for Polish crops - ministry.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish grain grew quickly from the start of May with unseasonably warm weather rapidly developing crops which were hard-hit by the long winter and cold spring, an Agriculture Ministry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Bozena Nowicka, deputy head of the production department, told PAP news agency that in many parts of the country crop conditions improved over the first two weeks of May and were nearly equal to five-year averages.</p>
<p>Nowicka said however that in some areas, where winter grain and rape seed sowings had been destroyed, crops were still developing slower than in past years.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
